# What the image build must not see.
#
# The rule is not "exclude junk" but "the image must be a function of tracked
# source and nothing else". Every entry here is something that exists on a
# developer's disk and would make a locally-built image differ from one built in
# CI from a clean clone — which is the failure where "it works on my machine"
# becomes "the image is not reproducible".

.git
.gitattributes
.github
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Credentials. The image must never contain them, and COPY is not a place to
# rely on a .gitignore.
.deploy.env
.env
*.env
!deploy/env.example

# Python build artefacts
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
build
dist
.venv
venv

# Local substrate state and experiment scratch
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.log
experiments/results/_cache
experiments/results/_dbg*
experiments/results/_sanity
experiments/results/_replay*

# Deployment descriptors are read by the deploy tooling, not by the image
docker-compose.yml
deploy/
docs/
